      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not define a synaptic transmitter as a general chemical signal that activates communication between cells; it only discusses cholinergic synapses and the energetic cost of packaging synaptic transmitter in the context of high-frequency firing.",
        "The claim that a synaptic transmitter \"must be packaged and supplied\" to support repeated high-frequency synaptic activity is too strong for the source; the article says packaging of synaptic transmitter may substantially exceed direct electrocyte costs, not that this is a defined requirement of the term itself.",
        "The definition mixes a broad textbook-style meaning with a narrow, article-specific energetic role, so the requested sense is not cleanly supported by the packet."
